### person-service — example requests
# person/person-service-with-loco — "person-style" layout (src/api/rest/).
# Envelope: {"success":bool,"data":...,"error":{"code","message","details"}}
# — data/error are ALWAYS both present (never omitted), src/api/mod.rs.
# Gated by PERSON_REQUIRE_AUTH (default off — see 00-auth-handshake.http
# for how to mint a bearer token once it's on).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8081
@personId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@otherPersonId = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@token = REPLACE_WITH_BEARER_FROM_00-auth-handshake.http


### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health


### Who am I — auth introspection. UNLIKE the rest of this file, whoami
# always requires a valid bearer token (its own AuthUser extractor, not
# gated by PERSON_REQUIRE_AUTH) — confirmed live: even with the blanket
# guard off, this 401s ("missing authorization header") with no token.
# curl-verified: examples/compose/full-family.yml does not wire
# PERSON_PASETO_KEYS_URL at authentication-service, so even a real token
# minted by 00-auth-handshake.http fails here with "no verification key
# for kid ..." — a real gap in the demo compose, not a documentation slip.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/whoami
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### Create a person — minimal valid body (name + gender are the only
# fields with no #[serde(default)]; id defaults to a fresh UUID).
# @name createPerson
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/persons
Content-Type: application/json
Accepts-version: 1.0

{
  "name": { "use": "official", "family": "Smith", "given": ["Ada"] },
  "birth_date": "1990-05-15",
  "gender": "female"
}


### Get the created person back (swap in the id from createPerson's
# response `data.id` if your client doesn't chain requests).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/persons/{{personId}}


### Search persons — total/offset are reported in the JSON body
# (data.total / data.offset), not response headers, for this crate.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/persons/search?q=Smith&limit=10&offset=0


### Update a person
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/persons/{{personId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": { "use": "official", "family": "Smith", "given": ["Ada", "Jane"] },
  "birth_date": "1990-05-15",
  "gender": "female"
}


### Probabilistic + deterministic match — score a candidate against
# existing records without creating anything.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/persons/match
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": { "family": "Smith", "given": ["Ada"] },
  "birth_date": "1990-05-15",
  "gender": "female"
}


### Explicit duplicate check (does not create; same body shape as match)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/persons/check-duplicates
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": { "family": "Smith", "given": ["Ada"] },
  "birth_date": "1990-05-15",
  "gender": "female"
}


### Batch deduplicate — scans the whole index for candidate pairs
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/persons/deduplicate


### Review queue — list pending candidate pairs
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/persons/review-queue?status=pending


### Review queue — confirm or reject a pending item (first-writer-wins;
# only `pending` items can be decided). Replace {{reviewId}} with a real
# id from the previous request's response.
# POST {{baseUrl}}/api/persons/review-queue/{{reviewId}}/decision
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# { "status": "confirmed" }


### Merge two confirmed-duplicate records (destructive; needs two real
# pre-existing records — see agents/share/merge.md).
# POST {{baseUrl}}/api/persons/merge
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# { "main_id": "{{personId}}", "duplicate_id": "{{otherPersonId}}" }


### Cross-service link — assert same_identity to a worker record
# (cross-service-linking.md §9; person + worker are the only two crates
# that originate entity_links today).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/persons/{{personId}}/links
Content-Type: application/json

{ "kind": "same_identity", "to_ref": "worker:{{otherPersonId}}" }


### List this person's outbound links
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/persons/{{personId}}/links


### Masked view (privacy.md — sensitive fields redacted)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/persons/{{personId}}/masked


### GDPR export for this subject
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/persons/{{personId}}/export


### Audit trail for this record
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/persons/{{personId}}/audit


### Bulk import (JSONL) — 202 Accepted, returns a job id
# (bulk-import-export.md; person is the reference crate for bulk).
# POST {{baseUrl}}/api/persons/import
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# { "format": "jsonl", "dedupe_mode": "upsert" }


### FHIR R5 — read this person as a Patient resource
GET {{baseUrl}}/fhir/Patient/{{personId}}


### Delete (soft-delete) a person
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/persons/{{personId}}
